            "Most readers who stop after the first three books are happy. God Emperor and beyond are for people who want to see where Herbert's ideas went.",
            "Whichever way you go in, keep the appendices in mind. Herbert's glossary and his notes on the ecology, religion and great houses of the Imperium are part of the novel, and a quick look at them makes the opening chapters much less daunting. The 2021 film does something similar on screen, letting you learn the world through Paul's training rather than through exposition.",
